            <rect x="88" y="120" width="8" height="20" fill="var(--gold-deep)"/>
            <rect x="76" y="138" width="32" height="6" fill="var(--gold-deep)"/>
            <g fill="var(--green)">
              <circle cx="150" cy="60" r="9"/><circle cx="166" cy="66" r="9"/><circle cx="140" cy="74" r="9"/>
              <circle cx="158" cy="80" r="9"/><circle cx="174" cy="86" r="9"/><circle cx="148" cy="94" r="9"/>
            </g>
            <path d="M150,50 Q158,36 172,40" fill="none" stroke="var(--green)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <span class="tag"><span class="lang-es">Enoturismo · desde 2014</span><span class="lang-en">Wine tourism · since 2014</span></span>
        <h3><span class="lang-es">Valle de Curicó</span><span class="lang-en">Curicó Valley</span></h3>
        <p>
          <span class="lang-es">Viñedos, bodegas, elaboración de vinos, degustaciones y paisajes rurales, con viñas como Miguel Torres, San Pedro, Aresti, Valdivieso y Requingua, además de Millaman en el sector de Los Niches. El 23 de enero de 2014 se formalizó el Organismo de Gestión de Destino Curicó Valle y Cordillera.</span>
          <span class="lang-en">Vineyards, wineries, winemaking, tastings, and rural landscapes, with wineries such as Miguel Torres, San Pedro, Aresti, Valdivieso and Requingua, as well as Millaman in the Los Niches area. On January 23, 2014, the Curicó Valley and Mountains Destination Management Organization was formally established.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="territorio">
